First of all what is SLAM; Silmultanious Localization and Mapping - Exists as a a solution to the chicken and egg problem made by localisation and mapping;

- A map is required to localize the robot accurately.
- A localised pose is required to build a map. 

This confrence paper is a summery of a SLAM system that couples localisation with volumetric occupancy mapping to fuse depth and uncertantiy predictions.

"~ Our method is rigourously uncertantiy aware: first we use depth and uncertanity predictions from a deep network...fuse motion stereo...provides depth information aross a range of baselines...increasing mapping accuracy"

A map is a the environments structure from a known location.
A pose is the estimation of a robots coordiantes (x,y,z) and oriantation (roll, pitch, yaw).
A voxel is a 3D data poiny on a regular grid, analogous to a 2D pixel

